{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y5btKhsVXAGjjeK2xgu7kb","type":"tool_result","content":"artifacts/weighting/__init__.py\nartifacts/weighting/alpha_eff.py\nartifacts/detector/train_detector.py\nartifacts/evaluation/eval_pipeline.py\nartifacts/evaluation/compare_results.py\nartifacts/data_generation/generate_synthetic.py\nauto_eval_watcher.py\nartifacts/training/extract_train_metrics.py\nanalyze_mvp.py\nartifacts/training/pretrain_weighted.py"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LW8mbrieEKz4xgatAsj4cC","session_id":"8f6920ef-6781-4109-a7b5-010e193d10d8","uuid":"3ce8808c-89fb-46d9-97a2-3c5e5ece93af","timestamp":"2026-05-15T02:14:25.370Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01XArsiVsmg9AZyJTDip2D7j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ary1Xz6F5GeW2mATGqp1cc","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 2 (R2) for a top ML venue review. Your focus areas are **Novelty** and **Related Work**. Review the paper described below independently. Do NOT consult other reviewers. Use a 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept. Target venue acceptance rate ~25%.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title:** Adaptive Contamination-Aware Reweighting for Pretraining on Mixed Real-Synthetic Corpora\n\n**Core idea:** The paper proposes \"adaptive b*\", replacing the fixed exponent b in the weighting function w=(1-q)^b (from Drayson et al. 2025) with a per-batch optimized value. b* is derived by maximizing an effective power-law index α_eff(b) subject to an ESS (effective sample size) constraint ESS(b) ≥ n_min. This eliminates grid search over b.\n\n**Claimed contributions:**\n1. Theoretical framework: α_eff(b) estimation + ESS constraints → principled b derivation from batch statistics alone. No validation set, no grid search, no known contamination ratio needed.\n2. Practical result: Adaptive b* matches grid-search-optimal at zero tuning cost (6N→1 run). Lightweight detector (TF-IDF+LR, AUC=0.939) suffices.\n3. Problem setting: One-pass web pretraining with unknown contamination proportion (vs Drayson's recursive training setting).\n\n**Related work cited:**\n- Shumailov et al. 2024 (model collapse from recursive synthetic data, Nature)\n- Convergence Theory 2025 (convergence bounds motivating α_eff)\n- Drayson et al. 2025 (detect-and-reweight with w=(1-q)^b, SIR resampling, EMNLP)\n- Golden Ratio Weighting 2025 (theoretically optimal weight, requires known contamination ratio k)\n- DoReMi (Xie et al. 2023, domain-level weights, NeurIPS)\n- DSIR (Xie et al. 2023, importance resampling, NeurIPS)\n- SoftDedup (Abbas et al. 2024, deduplication via soft similarity, ACL)\n- Dynamic Loss 2025 (loss-based reweighting without detector, ICLR)\n\n**Method details:**\n- Weighted loss: L_b = (1/|B|) Σ (1-q_i)^b · ℓ(x_i; θ)\n- b* = argmax_b α_eff(b) s.t. ESS(b) ≥ n_min\n- ESS(b) = (Σ w_i)² / Σ w_i², w_i = (1-q_i)^b\n- Graceful degradation: if no feasible b>0, set b*=0 (uniform)\n- Sole hyperparameter: n_min=2\n\n**Key results:**\n- Aggregate ratio 85.8% of grid-best improvement\n- PPL landscape flat in b=0.1–0.5 (range 0.014 PPL)\n- Lightweight detector sufficiency (AUC 0.939 vs 0.986 → only 0.005 PPL diff)\n- Effect amplifies with contamination ratio and model size (both 2×)\n- Weak points: cross-generator (75% ratio), domain-skewed (50% ratio), no significant downstream\n\n**Experimental context:** All experiments use 132M–200M tokens on Qwen3-0.6B (primary) and Llama-3.2-3B. Batch size 4. The paper covers all imagined experiments from the design document.\n\n## Your Review Task (R2: Novelty and Related Work)\n\nEvaluate:\n\n1. **Novelty assessment**: Is adaptive b* a genuine contribution or an obvious/incremental extension of Drayson et al.? The core idea is: take the existing w=(1-q)^b, replace fixed b with per-batch optimization via α_eff + ESS. How novel is this?\n\n2. **Theoretical depth**: The α_eff(b) concept is introduced but how rigorously is it developed? Is the connection to power-law theory well-established or superficial? The paper describes Algorithm 1 in 7 lines — is the theoretical contribution thin?\n\n3. **Related work coverage**: Are important baselines missing? Consider:\n   - Other data weighting methods in pretraining\n   - Importance weighting in ML broadly (importance sampling literature)\n   - Curriculum learning connections\n   - Other contamination detection/mitigation approaches\n   - The ESS constraint is standard in importance sampling — is this connection acknowledged?\n\n4. **Positioning vs Drayson et al.**: The paper positions itself as complementary (one-pass vs recursive). Is this distinction meaningful? Does the paper adequately differentiate from simply \"automating b selection for Drayson's framework\"?\n\n5. **Claims vs evidence**: \"Principled derivation\" — is this justified? \"Zero tuning cost\" — but n_min is still a hyperparameter. \"Lightweight detector sufficiency\" — is this a contribution of the method or just an empirical observation?\n\n6. **Missing comparisons**: No comparison with Golden Ratio Weighting, DoReMi, DSIR, or other baselines beyond detect-and-remove and random reweighting. Is this a significant gap?\n\n7. **Scope of contribution**: Is this a paper-worthy contribution for a top venue, or is it better suited as a workshop paper / short paper?\n\nProvide your review in this format:\n```\n### R2 Review: Novelty and Related Work\n\n**Summary:** (2-3 sentences)\n\n**Strengths:**\n- S1: ...\n- S2: ...\n- ...\n\n**Weaknesses:**\n- W1: ...\n- W2: ...\n- ...\n\n**Questions for Authors:**\n- Q1: ...\n- ...\n\n**Minor Issues:**\n- ...\n\n**Score:** X/6\n**Confidence:** X/5\n**Justification:** (2-3 sentences explaining score)\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":827,"cache_read_input_tokens":56151,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":827},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f6920ef-6781-4109-a7b5-010e193d10d8","uuid":"16272509-dfae-4e29-9c79-9280439f3cf6"}
