{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EqR4htbtBC727FzeFFEjJc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# MVP Analysis Summary — Provenance Weight Training\n2\t\n3\t**Date**: 2026-05-14  \n4\t**Model**: Qwen3-0.6B, 200M tokens, contamination_ratio=0.4  \n5\t**Eval**: held-out human perplexity (4.08M tokens)\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## 1. Method × Seed Comparison (eval_ppl)\n10\t\n11\t| Method | seed42 | seed123 | seed456 | Mean | Std |\n12\t|--------|--------|---------|---------|------|-----|\n13\t| uniform | 17.690 | 17.690 | 17.700 | 17.693 | 0.006 |\n14\t| grid-best (b=0.5) | 17.651 | 17.638 | 17.650 | 17.646 | 0.007 |\n15\t| adaptive (n_min=3) | 17.690 | 17.630 | 17.640 | 17.653 | 0.033 |\n16\t| adaptive_fix (n_min=2) | 17.650 | 17.643 | 17.660 | 17.651 | 0.009 |\n17\t\n18\t---\n19\t\n20\t## 2. Grid-b Curve Data\n21\t\n22\t| b | seed42 | seed123 | seed456 |\n23\t|---|--------|---------|---------|\n24\t| 0.5 | 17.651 | 17.638 | 17.650 |\n25\t| 1.0 | 17.692 | 17.674 | 17.680 |\n26\t| 1.5 | 17.718 | 17.701 | 17.710 |\n27\t| 2.0 | 17.741 | 17.725 | *RUNNING* |\n28\t| 3.0 | 17.774 | 17.760 | *RUNNING* |\n29\t| 5.0 | 17.818 | 17.804 | *RUNNING* |\n30\t\n31\t三个 seed 前三个 b 值均呈单调递增：b 越大 PPL 越高，best-b=0.5 在搜索边界。seed456 与 seed42/123 趋势完全一致。\n32\t\n33\t---\n34\t\n35\t## 3. MVP Judgment (adaptive_fix vs grid-best)\n36\t\n37\t### Per-seed calculation\n38\t\n39\t| Metric | seed42 | seed123 | seed456 |\n40\t|--------|--------|---------|---------|\n41\t| uniform_ppl | 17.690 | 17.690 | 17.700 |\n42\t| grid_best_ppl (b=0.5) | 17.651 | 17.638 | 17.650 |\n43\t| adaptive_fix_ppl | 17.650 | 17.643 | 17.660 |\n44\t| Δ_grid = uniform - grid_best | 0.039 | 0.052 | 0.050 |\n45\t| Δ_adaptive_fix = uniform - adaptive_fix | 0.040 | 0.047 | 0.040 |\n46\t| ratio = Δ_adaptive_fix / Δ_grid | **102.6%** | **90.4%** | **80.0%** |\n47\t\n48\t### Aggregate (3 seeds) — Final\n49\t\n50\t| Metric | Value |\n51\t|--------|-------|\n52\t| Mean Δ_grid | 0.0470 |\n53\t| Mean Δ_adaptive_fix | 0.0423 |\n54\t| Mean ratio (ratio of means) | **90.1%** |\n55\t| Mean ratio (mean of per-seed ratios) | **91.0%** |\n56\t| D019 precise calculation (from eval_loss) | **88.6%** |\n57\t| Threshold | ≥ 90% |\n58\t| **Verdict** | **Path B PASS** (D019) |\n59\t\n60\tseed456 ratio (80.0%) 拉低了 aggregate。D019 基于更精确的 eval_loss 值计算得到 88.6%，采用 Path B 三支柱论证通过 MVP。详见 §7。\n61\t\n62\t---\n63\t\n64\t## 4. b* Distribution Cross-Seed Consistency\n65\t\n66\t> ⚠️ **数据修正 (2026-05-15)**: 原统计量因 eval checkpoint 记录（b*=0）混入训练统计而严重偏差。以下为排除 eval 记录后的修正值。\n67\t\n68\t| Statistic | seed42 | seed123 | seed456 | Cross-seed mean | CV |\n69\t|-----------|--------|---------|---------|-----------------|-----|\n70\t| count (training-only) | 26,458 | 25,906 | 26,396 | — | — |\n71\t| mean | 1.399 | 1.431 | 1.416 | 1.415 | 1.1% |\n72\t| median | 0.871 | 0.880 | 0.880 | 0.877 | 0.6% |\n73\t| std | 1.933 | 2.029 | 1.993 | 1.985 | 2.5% |\n74\t| pct_below_0.5 | 20.9% | 20.9% | 20.9% | 20.9% | ~0% |\n75\t| pct_0.5_to_1 | 35.7% | 35.7% | 35.7% | 35.7% | ~0% |\n76\t| pct_1_to_2 | 27.3% | 27.3% | 27.3% | 27.3% | ~0% |\n77\t| pct_above_2 | 16.1% | 16.1% | 16.1% | 16.1% | ~0% |\n78\t\n79\t- **所有统计量跨 seed 极其稳定**（CV ≤ 2.5%），b* 由数据分布和检测器决定，对训练随机性完全不敏感。\n80\t- **~79% 的 batch 获得 moderate-to-strong downweighting (b*≥0.5)**，仅 ~21% 给低权重（b*<0.5），其中仅 ~2% 为 b*=0（等价于 uniform）。\n81\t- 多数 batch（~36%）落在 b*∈[0.5, 1.0) 的主体区间，接受适度降权。约 16% 获得强降权（b*>2）。\n82\t- 方法不是\"大部分 batch 不加权\"，而是\"几乎所有 batch 都接受非零降权，力度由 batch 内污染分布决定\"。\n83\t\n84\t---\n85\t\n86\t## 5. Risks & Caveats\n87\t\n88\t1. **best-b 在搜索边界 (b=0.5)**：两个完成 seed 的 grid search 最优均为 b=0.5（最小搜索值）。真正的最优可能在 b<0.5。若扩展搜索至 b∈{0.1, 0.2, 0.3}，grid-best 可能更优，MVP ratio 可能下降。\n89\t\n90\t2. **train_loss 跨方法不可比**：uniform 使用标准 CE，grid-b/adaptive 使用 weighted CE（加权后 loss 值域不同）。eval_ppl 是唯一可比指标。\n91\t\n92\t3. **b* 分布特征**（数据修正后）：median b*≈0.88，~79% 的 batch 获得 b*≥0.5 的非平凡降权。仅 ~2% 的 batch 为 b*=0（等价 uniform）。方法对几乎所有 batch 施加适度降权，改善来自广泛的精细化加权而非少数极端 batch 的选择性处理。在更干净数据（低 contamination ratio）上，b* 分布可能整体左移，降权力度减弱。\n93\t\n94\t4. **seed456 grid-best 已完成，aggregate 降至 88.6%**：seed456 grid-best=17.650（ratio=80.0%）如预期拉低了 aggregate。D019 决策采用 Path B 三支柱论证通过 MVP。seed456 b=2.0/3.0/5.0 仍在跑，但不影响 grid-best（b=0.5 趋势已确认）。\n95\t\n96\t5. **改善绝对值小**：uniform→grid-best 仅降低 ~0.04-0.05 PPL（相对改善 ~0.26-0.29%）。在更大规模或更高污染率下效果是否放大有待验证。\n97\t\n98\t---\n99\t\n100\t## 6. Summary\n101\t\n102\t| Question | Answer |\n103\t|----------|--------|\n104\t| adaptive_fix 是否通过 MVP (≥90% of grid-best)? | **Path B PASS** (D019: aggregate 88.6%, 采用三支柱论证) |\n105\t| adaptive_fix 是否需要 grid search? | **NO** (zero hyperparameter tuning) |\n106\t| adaptive_fix vs adaptive (原版) 哪个更好? | adaptive_fix 在 seed42 上明显更好 (17.65 vs 17.69)，其他 seed 相当 |\n107\t| 是否需要扩展 grid search 范围? | **建议**：b<0.5 区间可能有更好的 grid-best |\n108\t| seed456 结果是否改变了结论? | **是，aggregate 从 95.6% 降至 88.6%**。seed456 ratio=80% 拉低了整体。但 3/3 seeds adaptive_fix > uniform，方法稳定。采用 Path B 通过。 |\n109\t\n110\t---\n111\t\n112\t## 7. Seed456 结果的两条叙事预案\n113\t\n114\t### ~~路径 A: Aggregate ≥ 90%~~ （未达到）\n115\t\n116\t### ✅ 路径 B: Aggregate 88.6% → MVP PASS（D019 决策）\n117\t- grid_best_seed456 = 17.650，Δ_grid = 0.050\n118\t- seed456 ratio = 80.0%，拉低 aggregate 至 88.6%（< 90% 阈值）\n119\t- **采用三支柱论证**：\n120\t  1. **Per-seed 100% consistency**：3/3 seeds adaptive_fix > uniform（无一例外）\n121\t  2. **adaptive ≈ grid-best within seed variance**：adaptive_fix 与 grid-best 差异在 seed 间方差范围内（seed std ~0.009 PPL）\n122\t  3. **消除 grid search 的实用价值**：adaptive 方法需 0 次超参搜索 vs grid 需 6×N_seeds 次训练（18 runs），计算成本降低 6×\n123\t- 这个 claim 比\"捕获 90% 改善量\"更稳健，不依赖精确的百分比阈值\n124\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LW8mbrieEKz4xgatAsj4cC","session_id":"8f6920ef-6781-4109-a7b5-010e193d10d8","uuid":"8765271f-aa5f-4d58-a0f4-f3ae75287778","timestamp":"2026-05-15T02:14:50.260Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R5X81t1N1PgD7rEJUnstq8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Convergence-theoretic adaptive contamination reweighting.\n2\t\n3\tImplements the effective authenticity rate α_eff(b) and related quantities\n4\tfor importance-weighted pretraining on contaminated corpora.\n5\t\n6\tKey idea: given a detector that outputs per-sample synthetic probability q_i,\n7\tassign weight w_i = (1 − q_i)^b. The parameter b controls the bias-variance\n8\ttradeoff: higher b downweights suspected synthetic data more aggressively\n9\tbut reduces effective sample size (ESS).\n10\t\n11\tCore quantities:\n12\t  α_eff(b) = Σ (1−q_i)^{b+1} / Σ (1−q_i)^b    — effective authenticity rate\n13\t  ESS(b)   = (Σ w_i)² / Σ w_i²                  — effective sample size\n14\t  b*       = inf{b ≥ 0 : α_eff(b) ≥ τ} s.t. ESS(b*) ≥ n_min\n15\t\n16\tReferences:\n17\t  - arXiv 2602.16065 (convergence bounds for weighted pretraining)\n18\t  - Drayson et al., EMNLP 2025 (grid-search weighting baseline)\n19\t\n20\tInputs:  q_scores ∈ [0,1]^N (synthetic probabilities from detector)\n21\tOutputs: weights w ∈ R_+^N (normalized to sum to N)\n22\t\"\"\"\n23\t\n24\timport math\n25\timport torch\n26\t\n27\t\n28\tdef compute_alpha_eff(q_scores: torch.Tensor, b: float) -> float:\n29\t    \"\"\"Effective authenticity rate α_eff(b) = Σ (1−q)^{b+1} / Σ (1−q)^b.\n30\t\n31\t    Properties:\n32\t      α_eff(0) = 1 − ρ̂  (unweighted authenticity)\n33\t      α_eff(b) → 1 as b → ∞\n34\t      α_eff(b) is monotonically non-decreasing in b\n35\t    \"\"\"\n36\t    q = q_scores.clamp(0.0, 1.0).double()\n37\t    one_minus_q = 1.0 - q\n38\t\n39\t    if b == 0.0:\n40\t        return float(one_minus_q.mean())\n41\t\n42\t    log_omq = torch.log(one_minus_q.clamp(min=1e-30))\n43\t    log_w = b * log_omq\n44\t    log_w_shift = log_w - log_w.max()\n45\t    w = torch.exp(log_w_shift)\n46\t\n47\t    numerator = (w * one_minus_q).sum()\n48\t    denominator = w.sum()\n49\t\n50\t    if denominator < 1e-30:\n51\t        return 1.0\n52\t\n53\t    return float(numerator / denominator)\n54\t\n55\t\n56\tdef compute_ess(q_scores: torch.Tensor, b: float) -> float:\n57\t    \"\"\"Effective sample size ESS(b) = (Σ w_i)² / Σ w_i².\n58\t\n59\t    ESS = N when b=0 (uniform weights), decreases as b increases.\n60\t    \"\"\"\n61\t    if b == 0.0:\n62\t        return float(q_scores.numel())\n63\t\n64\t    q = q_scores.clamp(0.0, 1.0).double()\n65\t    one_minus_q = 1.0 - q\n66\t\n67\t    log_omq = torch.log(one_minus_q.clamp(min=1e-30))\n68\t    log_w = b * log_omq\n69\t    log_w_shift = log_w - log_w.max()\n70\t    w = torch.exp(log_w_shift)\n71\t\n72\t    sum_w = w.sum()\n73\t    sum_w2 = (w * w).sum()\n74\t\n75\t    if sum_w2 < 1e-30:\n76\t        return 0.0\n77\t\n78\t    return float((sum_w * sum_w) / sum_w2)\n79\t\n80\t\n81\tdef find_optimal_b(\n82\t    q_scores: torch.Tensor,\n83\t    tau: float,\n84\t    n_min: int,\n85\t    b_max: float = 20.0,\n86\t    resolution: int = 1000,\n87\t) -> float:\n88\t    \"\"\"Find b* = inf{b ≥ 0 : α_eff(b) ≥ τ} subject to ESS(b*) ≥ n_min.\n89\t\n90\t    When the batch is clean enough (ρ̂ < 1 − τ), returns b=0 (uniform).\n91\t    When the ESS constraint conflicts with the α_eff threshold, returns\n92\t    b* = argmax_b α_eff(b) s.t. ESS(b) ≥ n_min.\n93\t    \"\"\"\n94\t    alpha_0 = compute_alpha_eff(q_scores, 0.0)\n95\t    if alpha_0 >= tau:\n96\t        return 0.0\n97\t\n98\t    n = q_scores.numel()\n99\t    if n_min > n:\n100\t        n_min = n\n101\t\n102\t    # Phase 1: grid search to find the feasible region\n103\t    grid = torch.linspace(0.0, b_max, resolution + 1).tolist()\n104\t\n105\t    best_feasible_b = 0.0\n106\t    best_feasible_alpha = alpha_0\n107\t    threshold_b = None\n108\t\n109\t    for b_val in grid:\n110\t        ess = compute_ess(q_scores, b_val)\n111\t        if ess < n_min:\n112\t            break\n113\t\n114\t        alpha = compute_alpha_eff(q_scores, b_val)\n115\t\n116\t        if alpha > best_feasible_alpha:\n117\t            best_feasible_alpha = alpha\n118\t            best_feasible_b = b_val\n119\t\n120\t        if alpha >= tau and threshold_b is None:\n121\t            threshold_b = b_val\n122\t\n123\t    if threshold_b is not None:\n124\t        # Phase 2: refine with bisection\n125\t        lo = max(0.0, threshold_b - b_max / resolution)\n126\t        hi = threshold_b\n127\t        for _ in range(50):\n128\t            mid = (lo + hi) / 2.0\n129\t            if compute_alpha_eff(q_scores, mid) >= tau:\n130\t                hi = mid\n131\t            else:\n132\t                lo = mid\n133\t        b_star = hi\n134\t        if compute_ess(q_scores, b_star) >= n_min:\n135\t            return b_star\n136\t\n137\t    return best_feasible_b\n138\t\n139\t\n140\tdef compute_sample_weights(q_scores: torch.Tensor, b: float) -> torch.Tensor:\n141\t    \"\"\"Per-sample weights w_i = (1−q_i)^b, normalized to sum to N.\"\"\"\n142\t    n = q_scores.numel()\n143\t\n144\t    if b == 0.0:\n145\t        return torch.ones_like(q_scores)\n146\t\n147\t    q = q_scores.clamp(0.0, 1.0)\n148\t    one_minus_q = 1.0 - q\n149\t\n150\t    log_omq = torch.log(one_minus_q.clamp(min=1e-30))\n151\t    log_w = b * log_omq\n152\t    log_w = log_w - log_w.max()\n153\t    w = torch.exp(log_w)\n154\t\n155\t    w = w * (n / w.sum().clamp(min=1e-30))\n156\t    return w.to(q_scores.dtype)\n157\t\n158\t\n159\tdef compute_concentration_bound(\n160\t    q_scores: torch.Tensor, b: float, delta: float = 0.05\n161\t) -> float:\n162\t    \"\"\"Concentration bound |α̂_eff − α_eff| ≤ O(√(w_max / (ESS · Σw))) · log(1/δ)).\n163\t\n164\t    Returns the upper bound on estimation error for α_eff with probability 1−δ.\n165\t    \"\"\"\n166\t    if b == 0.0:\n167\t        n = q_scores.numel()\n168\t        return float(math.sqrt(math.log(2.0 / delta) / (2.0 * n)))\n169\t\n170\t    q = q_scores.clamp(0.0, 1.0).double()\n171\t    one_minus_q = 1.0 - q\n172\t    log_omq = torch.log(one_minus_q.clamp(min=1e-30))\n173\t    log_w = b * log_omq\n174\t    log_w = log_w - log_w.max()\n175\t    w = torch.exp(log_w)\n176\t\n177\t    sum_w = w.sum()\n178\t    w_max = w.max()\n179\t    ess = compute_ess(q_scores, b)\n180\t\n181\t    if ess < 1e-10 or sum_w < 1e-30:\n182\t        return float(\"inf\")\n183\t\n184\t    bound = float(torch.sqrt(w_max / (ess * sum_w))) * math.log(2.0 / delta)\n185\t    return bound\n186\t\n187\t\n188\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n189\t    torch.manual_seed(42)\n190\t    n = 1000\n191\t\n192\t    # Simulate: 80% human (low q), 20% synthetic (high q)\n193\t    q_human = torch.rand(800) * 0.2\n194\t    q_synth = 0.7 + torch.rand(200) * 0.3\n195\t    q_scores = torch.cat([q_human, q_synth])\n196\t    q_scores = q_scores[torch.randperm(n)]\n197\t\n198\t    print(f\"N = {n}, mean q = {q_scores.mean():.4f}\")\n199\t    print(f\"True contamination ≈ 20%\\n\")\n200\t\n201\t    for b in [0.0, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 5.0, 10.0]:\n202\t        alpha = compute_alpha_eff(q_scores, b)\n203\t        ess = compute_ess(q_scores, b)\n204\t        bound = compute_concentration_bound(q_scores, b)\n205\t        print(f\"b={b:5.1f}  α_eff={alpha:.4f}  ESS={ess:8.1f}  bound={bound:.6f}\")\n206\t\n207\t    print()\n208\t\n209\t    tau = 0.95\n210\t    n_min = 100\n211\t    b_star = find_optimal_b(q_scores, tau=tau, n_min=n_min)\n212\t    alpha_star = compute_alpha_eff(q_scores, b_star)\n213\t    ess_star = compute_ess(q_scores, b_star)\n214\t    print(f\"Optimal b* = {b_star:.4f}  (tau={tau}, n_min={n_min})\")\n215\t    print(f\"  α_eff(b*) = {alpha_star:.4f}\")\n216\t    print(f\"  ESS(b*)   = {ess_star:.1f}\")\n217\t\n218\t    weights = compute_sample_weights(q_scores, b_star)\n219\t    print(f\"\\nWeights: sum={weights.sum():.1f}, min={weights.min():.4f}, \"\n220\t          f\"max={weights.max():.4f}, std={weights.std():.4f}\")\n221\t\n222\t    # Verify monotonicity of α_eff\n223\t    bs = [i * 0.5 for i in range(21)]\n224\t    alphas = [compute_alpha_eff(q_scores, b) for b in bs]\n225\t    monotone = all(alphas[i] <= alphas[i + 1] + 1e-10 for i in range(len(alphas) - 1))\n226\t    print(f\"\\nα_eff monotonicity check: {'PASS' if monotone else 'FAIL'}\")\n227\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ary1Xz6F5GeW2mATGqp1cc","session_id":"8f6920ef-6781-4109-a7b5-010e193d10d8","uuid":"2505c797-558b-4dff-b071-f4203e01d174","timestamp":"2026-05-15T02:14:50.041Z"}
